      "derivation": "Every property is a single linear segment sampled on eighths, so each expected value is exact in binary floating point: rotation is 180p, rotationX is 90p, rotationY is -45 + 90p, and z is -100 + 200p. z is renderer metadata rather than a public output, so it must survive normalization instead of being dropped with the internal keys, which is why this case asserts the exact key set.",
