    "rig": {
      "description": "A three-bone forward-kinematics chain sampled across the same grid, so a broken parent accumulation drifts instead of failing at one endpoint.",
      "derivation": "Bone lengths are held at 70 and 56 while local rotations ramp 10 to 40 and 20 to 35, on a pelvis that ramps to x 120, y -20, rotation 45. A child's world transform is the parent's world transform plus its local offset rotated by the parent's world rotation. These values are computed from that formula rather than closed form, because cos and sin of non-right angles are irrational and only agree within the 1e-9 tolerance. The endpoint rotations 85 and 120 match the invariants fk_test.dart already asserts.",
